    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for assimp",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for assimp fixes the following issues\n\n- CVE-2025-2151: vulnerability affects the function Assimp: GetNextLine in the library ParsingUtils.h (bsc#1239220).\n- CVE-2025-2591: division by zero in code/AssetLib/MDL/MDLLoader.cpp (bsc#1239920).\n- CVE-2025-2592: heap-based buffer overflow in Assimp: CSMImporter: InternReadFile of code/AssetLib/CSM/CSMLoader.cpp\n  (bsc#1239916).\n- CVE-2025-3015: manipulation of the argument mIndices leads to out-of-bounds read (bsc#1240412).\n- CVE-2025-3548: processing of malformed files may leads to an out-of-bounds read and potential application crash\n  (bsc#1241367).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
